 \"url\": \"https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog\"}}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"@id\": \"https://www.dijaedadula.com/crm-pipeline-stages-service-business#faq\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How many stages should a sales pipeline have for a service business?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Most service businesses work well with five to seven stages. Six common ones are new inquiry, qualified, call booked, proposal sent, decision, and won or lost. Add a stage only when different work happens there.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the difference between a pipeline stage and a status?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"A stage shows where a deal is in your sales process. A status shows whether it is still alive, for example open, won, lost or abandoned. Some CRMs combine the two by using won and lost as final stages.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Which pipeline stages can be automated?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The first reply, tagging, qualifying questions, booking, reminders and follow-ups are good candidates. Discovery calls, proposals, pricing and the decision to close a high-value deal as lost should stay with a person.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What should I measure in my sales pipeline?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Track stage conversion rate, median time in each stage and the number of stalled deals every week. Together they show where buyers drop out and where deals are waiting on your team.\"}}]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://www.dijaedadula.com/home\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"B